1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,212
Day 55: SenseNova-Loop-9B,

2
00:00:02,212 --> 00:00:07,146
a language model that runs the same block of layers twice.

3
00:00:07,146 --> 00:00:09,358
We changed how many times.

4
00:00:09,808 --> 00:00:12,568
It stores only 32 decoder layers,

5
00:00:12,568 --> 00:00:16,918
but runs layers 4 to 27 twice with the same weights,

6
00:00:16,918 --> 00:00:20,431
so every token gets 56 layer computations.

7
00:00:20,881 --> 00:00:23,355
Tokens go through the first four layers,

8
00:00:23,355 --> 00:00:25,026
then into the looped block.

9
00:00:25,476 --> 00:00:29,364
The block's output is fed back into the same layers once more

10
00:00:29,364 --> 00:00:31,149
before the last four layers.

11
00:00:31,149 --> 00:00:33,380
The loop count is a single setting,

12
00:00:33,380 --> 00:00:35,611
so we switched it from one to four.

13
00:00:36,061 --> 00:00:40,077
With one loop, it got only 1 of 20 multiplications right,

14
00:00:40,077 --> 00:00:40,992
down from 19.

15
00:00:40,992 --> 00:00:44,233
More loops did not help: four loops scored 11.

16
00:00:44,233 --> 00:00:48,530
The weights were trained for two passes, and two worked best.

17
00:00:48,980 --> 00:00:50,864
Apache 2.0, from SenseTime.

18
00:00:50,864 --> 00:00:55,189
Source, license and the full write-up are linked on GitHub and

19
00:00:55,189 --> 00:00:56,585
in the Zenn article.
